WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.603 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:04.837
-Hey, everybody.

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:09.675
Welcome to another episode
of "Summer Corrections."

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:12.178
Or, as we've taken to
calling it, "Summerections."

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.680
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.014
'Cause we love -- we love --

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:17.517
As we've established,
we love a portmanteau here.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.052
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.822
I will say...

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:25.325
I do find...

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:27.092
corrections
a little bit easier

00:00:27.092 --> 00:00:28.494
the rest of the year,

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:29.829
for whatever it's worth.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:32.198
I don't know
the difference, but...

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.867
Summerections are hard.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.635
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:41.607
So, I did -- since we missed
"Corrections" last week,

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:45.878
I missed Wednesday, Thursday
of last week

00:00:45.878 --> 00:00:47.113
and Monday, Tuesday this week

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.549
because I tested positive
for COVID

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.718
last Wednesday morning.

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.119
And then, but I wanted
to come back.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.388
I wanted to do
the two shows this week.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.823
I'm very happy that we did.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:01:00.493
I wanted to make sure that
it was safe before I came back.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:03.095
So I went to the CDC website,

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:05.198
and I don't know if you've gone
and checked it recently,

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:07.333
but it just said,
"Ehh, do whatever you want."

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.001
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:12.205
"You're not gonna listen.
Just do whatever you want."

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:15.207
"You don't have an aunt
who's been googling

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:18.144
you can check with?"

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.813
Oh, this is interesting.

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:22.148
We talked about Mac Tonight.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.883
We've been talking
a little bit about Mac Tonight.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:28.053
This was
a commercial spokesperson

00:01:28.053 --> 00:01:31.057
that was launched in 1987

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:34.794
because McDonald's wanted kids
to have more nightmares.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.629
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.732
And I guess the idea was that
it was this...

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.134
you know, the kids
would just be terrified.

00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:44.304
He had a piano.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:48.107
The keys were made
from the bones of his victims.

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:49.775
And it would just,
kids would be terrified

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:51.744
and then they would wake up
and they'd be super upset

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:55.481
if they had seen Mac Tonight
and then the only way to get

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:58.818
them to calm down
was to go to McDonald's.

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:00.853
Anyway, this is fascinating.
This is not a correction.

00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:02.588
This is just, again,
because I think at the end

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:04.290
we're trying to learn
with "Corrections," right?

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.959
I mean, that's what we've said.

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:12.298
Mac Tonight wasn't just like
a guy with a moon head on.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:16.335
He was a fantastic actor
named Doug Jones.

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:20.139
Doug Jones was
in "Shape of Water."

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:21.874
This is the same actor.

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:25.645
He was in "Pan's Labyrinth."
He played the faun.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.747
And so, he's this
wonderful actor, and this --

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:31.951
he got his start as Mac Tonight,
which is really cool.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.953
So, and this is
the really amazing thing, right?

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:36.856
So, first he was Mac Tonight.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:39.024
Then he was in "Shape of Water."

00:02:39.024 --> 00:02:40.326
In "The Shape of Water,"

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.794
the character
in "Shape of Water" --

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:44.296
I don't know if you remember
this -- but ended up

00:02:44.296 --> 00:02:45.798
as that.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:57.010
Full circle.

00:02:59.211 --> 00:03:01.281
This one I feel terrible about.

00:03:03.348 --> 00:03:07.052
We said that Rudy Giuliani
played "Wonderful Tonight"

00:03:07.052 --> 00:03:11.057
at his first wedding when
he married his second cousin.

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.959
That song came out in 1977.

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:16.428
The wedding was 1968.

00:03:16.428 --> 00:03:17.930
So, apologies to Rudy,

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:21.234
as well as to the daughter
of his first cousin.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.802
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:28.607
And I didn't know
how long ago that was

00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:31.443
when Rudy married his cousin,

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:33.979
because 1968
was a different time.

00:03:33.979 --> 00:03:36.349
Still weird
to marry your cousin.

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:43.756
I meant to say that that
an image was Photoshop friendly,

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.758
but I said it was
friendly Photoshop.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.594
Me just ad-libbing, and
sometimes I say things wrong.

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:51.631
Also, that's just an age thing.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.232
'Cause when we grew up,

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.935
Shoemaker and I,
when we grew up, like,

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:59.038
Photoshop wasn't a thing
you would do on your computer.

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.874
You would go to your friendly
neighborhood Photoshop.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.375
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:05.878
And do it all by hand.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:08.381
You wouldn't just, like,
email Tara and say,

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:09.615
"Do this, make this image."

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:11.617
You would have to, like,
go down to the shop.

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:13.119
Carson, Johnny Carson,
would do it all the time.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:14.787
He'd have to go to Burbank.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.222
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:19.425
"Can you, uh,

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:22.395
put Richard Nixon
in a prison uniform for me?"

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.230
And they'd be like, "When do you
need it by, Mr. Carson?"

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.564
He's like, "I'd love it
for tonight's show."

00:04:25.564 --> 00:04:28.100
"It's gonna be --
it'll be weeks.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.802
It's gonna take weeks."

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:34.573
One of you said...

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:37.576
Did a joke about Donald Trump
getting an ice cream headache

00:04:37.576 --> 00:04:40.779
from a Frosty at Wendy's.

00:04:40.779 --> 00:04:42.749
And you said you can't get

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.684
an ice cream headache
from a Frosty.

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:48.987
You can only get an ice cream
headache from an ice cream.

00:04:48.987 --> 00:04:51.824
So, if you're drinking a Frosty
and you say to a friend,

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.292
"I have an ice cream headache,"

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:54.693
and that friend is a jackal,

00:04:54.693 --> 00:04:57.130
they'll say to you,
"What'd ya get it from?"

00:04:58.297 --> 00:05:00.466
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.468
Oh, we were talking
about "Avatar."

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.137
It took six years in the film,

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:08.207
almost six years
to get to Pandora from Earth.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:13.012
So, that means you could
go to Pandora and back

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:15.014
before "Avatar Two" came out.

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.883
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.153
I do like to point out
when a jackal

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:24.023
writes something
that makes me smile.

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:26.692
And you said,
in James Cameron's defense,

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:28.494
the reason "Avatar Two"
is taking so long

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.663
is they're filming it
on location.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.432
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:41.574
I made a joke
in the last "Corrections"

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:43.342
where the punchline was
Kelly Rowland.

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:44.877
A lot of you didn't get it.

00:05:46.912 --> 00:05:49.148
I think just go back
and watch it again.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:51.483
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.483 --> 00:05:53.018
I could explain it,
but I just feel like

00:05:53.018 --> 00:05:55.054
it wouldn't be as satisfying.

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.793
Hey, this isn't gonna be --

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:02.128
I should note,
this is not gonna be

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:04.797
a particularly
long "Corrections" tonight.

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:09.067
But I do want to address...

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:10.169
the Emmys.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:13.506
The Emmys are coming up,
and "Corrections,"

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:15.874
as we know by now,
is Emmy-nominated.

00:06:15.874 --> 00:06:19.578
But I was thinking about
Emmy categories that I wish --

00:06:19.578 --> 00:06:21.614
when I had COVID
I watched a lot of TV --

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:24.617
Emmy categories
that I wish existed.

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:27.953
And here is an Emmy category
I wish existed.

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:32.125
It's the best line reading
on television this year.

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:33.459
It's the best pronunciation.

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:35.962
Let me specify
the best pronunciation of a word

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:37.597
that I had never heard
pronounced that way

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:38.931
on TV this year.

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:41.834
And the nominees are both
from "White Lotus."

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:44.069
The first nominee
is Molly Shannon

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:48.407
for the way she says
"palm fronds" in "White Lotus."

00:06:48.407 --> 00:06:50.075
Take a look.

00:06:50.075 --> 00:06:52.578
-[ Sighs ]
And all the palm fronds.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.814
-Very good.

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:57.316
But what about
how Jennifer Coolidge

00:06:57.316 --> 00:07:01.020
says "chaise lounge"
in "White Lotus?"

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.654
Let's take a look.

00:07:02.654 --> 00:07:04.590
-That chaise is taken.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.925
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.925 --> 00:07:08.661
-Impossible to choose.

00:07:13.098 --> 00:07:15.501
In our category,
"Corrections'" category...

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:18.504
I promised I wouldn't
politic too much, but...

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:21.607
It's us, "Tooning Out the News,"
Stephen Colbert,

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:23.776
"Carpool Karaoke,"

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:25.944
"Randy Rainbow,"

00:07:25.944 --> 00:07:28.080
and "I think You Should Leave
with Tim Robinson."

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.450
And, pains me to say it...

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:36.655
If you're wondering
who I think the winner is...

00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:39.958
to quote the great Bob Dylan,

00:07:39.958 --> 00:07:41.461
"It's not me, lady."

00:07:43.496 --> 00:07:44.997
It's Tim Robinson.

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:47.032
"I Think You Should Leave" is...

00:07:47.032 --> 00:07:49.401
"Coffin Flop" alone.

00:07:49.401 --> 00:07:50.903
It deserves the Emmy.

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:52.471
And if you haven't seen
"Coffin Flop,"

00:07:52.471 --> 00:07:54.239
go on Netflix and watch
"Coffin Flop."

00:07:54.239 --> 00:07:56.842
And, look,
I aspire for excellence

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:58.411
and I would -- I would love
to win an Emmy.

00:07:58.411 --> 00:08:01.514
But sometimes you have to say,
you know...

00:08:01.514 --> 00:08:03.049
tied for second.

00:08:06.252 --> 00:08:09.387
Hey, we're gonna be off
for all of August.

00:08:09.387 --> 00:08:11.857
This is not our fault.

00:08:11.857 --> 00:08:14.927
It's the fault of, really,
the summer TV viewer,

00:08:14.927 --> 00:08:17.663
who doesn't enjoy watching
television in the summer.

00:08:17.663 --> 00:08:19.165
And NBC executives
took us aside and said,

00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:21.167
"You know what people
want in the summer?

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:23.135
It's, like, more like
'FBOY Island'

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:25.504
and less like your show."

00:08:25.504 --> 00:08:27.673
And -- And we said,
"What if we made our show

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:30.076
a little bit more like
'FBOY Island'?"

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:31.743
And they said, "Well,
what's the closest thing

00:08:31.743 --> 00:08:33.145
you have to an F-boy?"

00:08:33.145 --> 00:08:34.980
And we said, "Scollins?"

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.983
And they said,
"Take off August."

00:08:36.983 --> 00:08:38.751
[ Laughter ]

00:08:43.856 --> 00:08:47.859
There's a conclusion of sorts
to the mug saga, you guys.

00:08:47.859 --> 00:08:49.628
You know, we...

00:08:49.628 --> 00:08:51.497
When we first came up
with this idea,

00:08:51.497 --> 00:08:54.934
the question was,
how hard is it to make a mug?

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:57.303
And the answer is,
"Remarkably."

00:08:57.303 --> 00:08:59.471
[ Laughter ]

00:08:59.471 --> 00:09:01.574
But after a lot of work,
this is -- you guys,

00:09:01.574 --> 00:09:03.442
this is now available
in the NBC Store.

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:05.677
It's the Late night
with Corrections Jackals mug.

00:09:05.677 --> 00:09:07.780
And there's a jackal over here.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:12.951
But there was a bit of drama,
you guys, with the mug.

00:09:12.951 --> 00:09:16.454
So, here's what happened.

00:09:16.454 --> 00:09:20.159
We were gonna announce the mug
two "Corrections" ago

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:23.429
and then, last minute,
I mentioned this on

00:09:23.429 --> 00:09:24.896
on that "Corrections."
Actually,

00:09:24.896 --> 00:09:26.699
it was one "Corrections,"
but two weeks ago.

00:09:26.699 --> 00:09:28.367
It was like, "Whoa, it's not
in the store yet.

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:29.902
Don't announce it."
So I didn't announce it.

00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:31.703
The last thing we want to do
is for you guys to,

00:09:31.703 --> 00:09:33.505
you know, clog up the internet
trying to buy these

00:09:33.505 --> 00:09:35.507
and they're not available yet.

00:09:35.507 --> 00:09:37.976
So we didn't announce it.
Then, obviously, I have COVID.

00:09:37.976 --> 00:09:41.146
In that time, though,
a really weird thing happened.

00:09:41.146 --> 00:09:43.382
They started selling
a different "Corrections" mug

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:45.384
at the NBC Store.

00:09:45.384 --> 00:09:48.321
It looked like this.

00:09:48.321 --> 00:09:52.091
There were actually two of them,
and that was at the NBC Store.

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:54.460
And so we were shocked
because we've had

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:56.094
a lot of conversations
about the mug

00:09:56.094 --> 00:09:58.063
and all of a sudden a mug
that I've never seen before

00:09:58.063 --> 00:09:59.564
was in the NBC Store.

00:09:59.564 --> 00:10:02.634
And our producer,
Eric Leiderman,

00:10:02.634 --> 00:10:04.636
he wrote me an email
about what had happened,

00:10:04.636 --> 00:10:07.206
and I was gonna read it to you.

00:10:08.807 --> 00:10:10.976
But I'm not going to,
because here's the thing.

00:10:10.976 --> 00:10:12.778
I'm not saying it's long...

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:16.281
[ Laughter ]

00:10:16.281 --> 00:10:18.417
But if I read you
the full email,

00:10:18.417 --> 00:10:19.985
we would all miss
the premiere

00:10:19.985 --> 00:10:21.821
of "Avatar Three."

00:10:21.821 --> 00:10:23.489
[ Laughter ]

00:10:25.758 --> 00:10:27.927
The thing is, I feel terrible,
but if you bought this mug,

00:10:27.927 --> 00:10:30.162
this is not an official
"Corrections" mug.

00:10:30.162 --> 00:10:31.964
You have -- I mean,
you have a mug, and it's --

00:10:31.964 --> 00:10:33.432
look, it says
"Corrections Jackal"

00:10:33.432 --> 00:10:34.866
and I hope you enjoy it,
but it's a little bit

00:10:34.866 --> 00:10:37.370
like, you know, you think
you bought a Chanel bag

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:38.704
and you get home and your
friend's like,

00:10:38.704 --> 00:10:40.473
"That says Channel."

00:10:40.473 --> 00:10:42.641
[ Laughter ]

00:10:42.641 --> 00:10:45.810
Also, you know...

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:47.613
I was looking on Etsy.

00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:48.980
Some people on Etsy

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:51.417
have just been making
their own "Corrections" mugs.

00:10:51.417 --> 00:10:52.818
That one's nice.

00:10:53.886 --> 00:10:56.255
That one's nice.
Got an Egyptian theme to it.

00:10:58.124 --> 00:11:00.292
This one's nice.

00:11:00.292 --> 00:11:02.594
So, I think
the important thing to note

00:11:02.594 --> 00:11:05.231
is this is...

00:11:05.231 --> 00:11:08.400
this is our segment
that we do every week,

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:10.068
and when it came
to making the mugs,

00:11:10.068 --> 00:11:11.937
we finished last.

00:11:11.937 --> 00:11:13.606
[ Laughter ]

00:11:16.608 --> 00:11:18.110
[ Clears throat ]

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:20.779
But, you know,
I think in the end, any --

00:11:20.779 --> 00:11:22.715
I think any mug
you want to buy for yourself

00:11:22.715 --> 00:11:24.883
that you think best represents
the kind of jackal you are,

00:11:24.883 --> 00:11:27.552
I think go for it,
because if we've learned

00:11:27.552 --> 00:11:29.321
anything from this journey
of "Corrections,"

00:11:29.321 --> 00:11:31.791
there are no right answers.

00:11:34.993 --> 00:11:37.262
But it's here.

00:11:37.262 --> 00:11:39.098
♪ Summer muggin' ♪

00:11:39.098 --> 00:11:42.267
[ Laughter ]

00:11:42.267 --> 00:11:44.136
♪ Happened so slow ♪

00:11:44.136 --> 00:11:45.671
[ Laughter ]

00:11:47.839 --> 00:11:49.508
♪ Tell me less, tell me less ♪

00:11:49.508 --> 00:11:50.943
[ Laughs ]

00:11:52.644 --> 00:11:53.912
That's great, though.

00:11:53.912 --> 00:11:55.514
We got our own mug.

00:11:55.514 --> 00:11:57.716
Come on, back me up, guys.

00:11:57.716 --> 00:11:59.151
This is really nice.

00:11:59.151 --> 00:12:02.154
This is really nice.
I will say...

00:12:02.154 --> 00:12:05.590
being right-handed,
I kind of prefer this side,

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:07.192
you know, and I was like,
as a righty,

00:12:07.192 --> 00:12:11.063
the side I like less
is facing out.

00:12:12.197 --> 00:12:14.766
So I said, "How hard
would it be...?"

00:12:14.766 --> 00:12:16.168
28 months.

00:12:16.168 --> 00:12:18.170
[ Laughter ]

00:12:25.243 --> 00:12:26.845
So, I...

00:12:26.845 --> 00:12:29.114
You know, I don't
want you to think --

00:12:29.114 --> 00:12:31.784
'cause sometimes
you all say, "Hey..."

00:12:33.953 --> 00:12:35.620
"Enjoying your summer vacation?"

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.455
No.

00:12:37.455 --> 00:12:39.524
I like it here.

00:12:39.524 --> 00:12:42.394
I like doing this.
I don't like being at the beach.

00:12:42.394 --> 00:12:45.264
I'm not being lazy.
Okay?

00:12:48.166 --> 00:12:53.272
But the important thing
is we were together today,

00:12:53.272 --> 00:12:57.109
we'll be together again
in September.

00:12:57.109 --> 00:13:01.180
Vote "I Think You Should
Leave with Tim Robinson."

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:03.849
Get whatever [bleep] mug
you want.

00:13:03.849 --> 00:13:05.384
[ Laughter ]

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:14.193
You know what really bums me out
about these Etsy people...

00:13:16.028 --> 00:13:18.364
...is their tiny little
pine cones.

00:13:18.364 --> 00:13:19.999
[ Laughter ]

00:13:22.735 --> 00:13:26.572
Like a couple of jackal's nuts.
[ Laughs ]

00:13:26.572 --> 00:13:29.241
They're -- They're just so...

00:13:29.241 --> 00:13:31.710
They're just so ahead of us.

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:34.747
And we're a major corporation.

00:13:34.747 --> 00:13:37.283
It took us like a year
to make a mug.

00:13:39.451 --> 00:13:41.787
Like this -- I want this mug
'cause I know, thanks to that,

00:13:41.787 --> 00:13:43.789
I know exactly how big it is.

00:13:43.789 --> 00:13:45.224
[ Laughter ]

00:13:47.793 --> 00:13:50.795
You guys,
have a wonderful summer.

00:13:50.795 --> 00:13:52.798
We love you very much.

00:13:52.798 --> 00:13:54.266
See me in September.

